STRATEGIC REASONING: {'The opponent\'s proposal includes items: B35, A10, C00, B86, A87, B32, C01, B41. I need to calculate its total effort and my total importance. Efforts: B35=140, A10=366, C00=665, B86=516, A87=319, B32=448, C01=825, B41=742. Total effort = 140+366+665+516+319+448+825+742 = 4021, which is under the limit of 4026. My importances: B35=262, A10=138, C00=121, B86=461, A87=668, B32=583, C01=389, B41=484. Total importance to me = 262+138+121+461+668+583+389+484 = 3106. I should compare this to my optimal set. My top items by importance/effort ratio: A77 (868/77=11.27), A04 (822/383=2.15), A03 (783/513=1.53), C17 (808/780=1.04), B33 (780/694=1.12), etc. But I must negotiate. The opponent\'s set is good for me (3106) but I might get more by including A77 (very high importance for low effort) and others. However, the opponent might value different items. I should propose a counter that includes my high-importance items while possibly accommodating the opponent\'s interests based on their proposal. They included many B items (B35, B86, B32, B41) and some A and C. I should propose a set that adds A77 and maybe A04, removing some lower-importance items for me. For example, remove C00 (121) and A10 (138) which are low for me, and add A77 (868) and A04 (822). But effort: current set 4021, remove C00 (665) and A10 (366) = 4021-665-366=2990, add A77 (77) and A04 (383) = 2990+77+383=3450, which is under. Then total importance for me: current 3106 -121-138 +868+822 = 4337, much better. But I need to see if it fits with opponent. Alternatively, I can propose a set that includes all their items except C00 and A10, plus A77 and A04. So set: {B35, B86, A87, B32, C01, B41, A77, A04}. Effort: 140+516+319+448+825+742+77+383 = 3450. My importance: 262+461+668+583+389+484+868+822 = 4537. This is much better for me. I should propose this, arguing it improves value without exceeding limit.'}

